  "notes": "Bhojpuri (Eastern UP and Bihar). Largest Indic diaspora language. Inherent vowel is /a/ (not /ə/ like Standard Hindi). No schwa deletion rule. Four-way laryngeal contrast. Retroflex series phonemic. This spec reads ⟨ऩ⟩, ⟨ऱ⟩ and ⟨ऴ⟩ as their base letters ⟨न⟩ [n], ⟨र⟩ [r] and ⟨ल⟩ [l], because the inventory has no separate phoneme for them. This spec has no ⟨ळ⟩, so ⟨ऴ⟩ takes the value of ⟨ल⟩.",
